1
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:38,680
What did No. 331 say to you?

2
00:02:38,760 --> 00:02:39,960
Why did you come here?

3
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,400
I was replaced.

4
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:43,160
No. 331 forfeited midway through.

5
00:02:43,240 --> 00:02:44,400
Do you know that?

6
00:02:47,040 --> 00:02:49,240
No. 331 ran 4.5 laps before forfeiting.

7
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:50,560
On the third lap,

8
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:52,200
No. 323 and No. 308 lapped her.

9
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:54,480
323 LI ZHENG, 308 ZHENG YU, 331 TONG RUYI

10
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:56,200
Are you sure?

11
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:58,120
No. 331 said she finished.

12
00:02:58,200 --> 00:03:00,040
Would she dare lie to a referee?

13
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:01,160
I'm sure.

14
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:03,200
No. 308 was the second finisher.

15
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:05,880
You can ask for an explanation
or check surveillance.

16
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:09,720
ZHENG YU, RANKING

17
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,400
Is that true?

18
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:19,360
RUNNING RESULTS

19
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:20,400
EVENT: 1500 M

20
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:21,480
ZHENG YU

21
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:24,960
Did the junior women's 1500 m
also take place today?

22
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:25,880
Yes.

23
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:28,360
Immediately after it was the men's 3000 m,

24
00:03:28,440 --> 00:03:29,960
then the women's 3000 m now.

25
00:03:44,480 --> 00:03:45,440
What's the problem?

26
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,400
I just ran.

27
00:03:48,760 --> 00:03:50,920
I'm nauseous and want to vomit.

28
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:53,920
If it's not serious,
just go back and rest.

29
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:54,840
It's serious.

30
00:03:59,440 --> 00:04:01,120
How many meters did you run?

31
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,120
The 3000 m.

32
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:03,640
And the 1500 m.

33
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:06,640
Do students this year
have to be so enthusiastic?

34
00:04:06,720 --> 00:04:09,640
He even has bruises from running.

35
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:15,240
Do you have omeprazole
or mosapride capsules?

36
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,160
Either will do.

37
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,320
Are you in the College of Medicine?

38
00:04:18,399 --> 00:04:19,640
Life Sciences.

39
00:04:22,640 --> 00:04:23,760
Register first.

40
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:26,800
Follow the instructions
for the usage and dosage.

41
00:04:26,880 --> 00:04:28,040
Okay.

42
00:04:32,160 --> 00:04:34,240
That's probably heatstroke.

43
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:35,760
Move him into the shade.

44
00:04:35,840 --> 00:04:37,160
Okay, I'll be right there.

45
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:41,560
- You can go after that.
- Thank you, miss.

46
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:54,120
ZHENG YU

47
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:18,000
Zheng Yu?

48
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:36,160
How do you feel?

49
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:39,280
Great.

50
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:41,000
Then why are you here?

51
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:46,160
I left right afterward.

52
00:05:46,240 --> 00:05:48,120
I didn't see my result.

53
00:05:49,640 --> 00:05:50,480
Am I second?

54
00:05:51,880 --> 00:05:52,920
Yes.

55
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,360
In the final sprint,

56
00:05:54,440 --> 00:05:56,760
No. 323 nearly lapped you.

57
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,520
Who is

58
00:06:06,600 --> 00:06:08,040
your box of medicine for?

59
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:12,640
Given your health condition,

60
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:14,920
you have no chance
of running long-distance.

61
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:17,920
What? Are you saving it for yourself?

62
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,320
I…

63
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:22,480
As a volunteer,

64
00:06:23,200 --> 00:06:25,040
I got it for athletes who need it.

65
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:27,560
Since you're fine, I'm leaving.

66
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:05,320
How

67
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:07,560
will you return to the dorm?

68
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:09,840
It's on my way.

69
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:12,520
I can take you with that.

70
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:14,760
Consider it volunteer duties.

71
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:18,640
My legs aren't crippled.

72
00:07:19,640 --> 00:07:22,000
Think of it as a means of transportation.

73
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:23,560
No.

74
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:28,640
Fine.

75
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:30,640
Then rest here.

76
00:07:31,240 --> 00:07:33,000
Your time isn't worth much anyway.

77
00:07:33,520 --> 00:07:34,600
It's fine to waste it.

78
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:47,880
It's your time that isn't worth much.

79
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:25,360
I can understand studying like crazy.

80
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:28,520
But going all out
for a sports meet in junior year?

81
00:08:29,120 --> 00:08:30,440
I can't figure out why.

82
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:31,960
It's to

83
00:08:32,039 --> 00:08:33,799
keep fit.

84
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:38,720
You don't think you're funny, do you?

85
00:08:39,720 --> 00:08:41,440
I'm saying this as your classmate.

86
00:08:42,280 --> 00:08:44,039
Save your energy for studying.

87
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:46,960
Otherwise, if I end up
winning the Vitality Award,

88
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:48,720
I will feel that I won unfairly.

89
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:55,120
Hello?

90
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:56,440
<i>I contacted No. 331.</i>

91
00:08:56,520 --> 00:08:59,200
<i>She admitted that she lied impulsively.</i>

92
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:02,200
<i>Forfeiting results in no score. That's it.</i>

93
00:09:02,280 --> 00:09:04,720
<i>Where are you? I need you</i>
<i>and Zhang Qi to sign.</i>

94
00:09:05,840 --> 00:09:07,360
Got it. I'll be right there.

95
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:10,840
I'll be okay.

96
00:09:12,880 --> 00:09:15,240
Do you know how to use this wheelchair?

97
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:22,520
I'm familiar with them.

98
00:09:23,840 --> 00:09:26,360
An old leg injury?

99
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:28,480
Then why did you race?

100
00:09:29,080 --> 00:09:30,680
I didn't need one myself.

101
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:32,160
I've watched others use them.

102
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:34,920
Who?

103
00:09:39,760 --> 00:09:41,000
Who else?

104
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:43,600
People who were injured

105
00:09:43,680 --> 00:09:44,680
and bedridden.

106
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:47,400
Wait.

107
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:49,400
You know how to use it.

108
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,600
You said nothing.

109
00:09:53,040 --> 00:09:55,960
You said you wanted
to fulfill your volunteer duties.

110
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:58,040
I couldn't interfere with your work.

111
00:10:16,960 --> 00:10:18,520
Zheng Yu, your feet!

112
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:21,480
- I'm fine.
- We'll help you upstairs.

113
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,080
No, thanks.

114
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,280
We're going to go.

115
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:30,280
Be careful.

116
00:10:37,680 --> 00:10:38,560
LIYUAN BUILDING 9

117
00:10:38,640 --> 00:10:39,480
Fangli.

118
00:10:40,040 --> 00:10:41,480
Why did you leave so quickly?

119
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:44,240
I said I wanted us to bond as roommates

120
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:46,920
and roped you guys into
giving her the shoes.

121
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,760
You all got humiliated with me.

122
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:50,600
What was humiliating about it?

123
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:53,520
Maybe Zheng Yu just thought that
the shoes were too expensive.

124
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:55,480
Didn't you say they were sold out?

125
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:57,440
She could have explained that to me.

126
00:10:58,640 --> 00:11:01,160
Anyway, if she ignores me,
I will ignore her.

127
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:03,040
Let's go get food.

128
00:11:35,160 --> 00:11:38,320
THE PRIZE MONEY FROM TODAY'S
SPORTS MEET HAS BEEN SENT.

129
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:47,880
Stop shaking it. Ma'am, that's enough.

130
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:48,800
Hello.

131
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:49,840
ATHLETE MEAL VOUCHER

132
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:52,080
Pick two meats and a vegetable.

133
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:54,000
- This.
- This.

134
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:55,160
And this.

135
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:11,120
I've never seen you at the cafeteria.

136
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:14,760
Except once.

137
00:12:16,560 --> 00:12:18,920
Are you back to volunteer again today?

138
00:12:20,480 --> 00:12:23,480
I came to campus today to go to the lab.

139
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:29,360
And on the way…

140
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:34,560
Your medals.

141
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:37,560
I grabbed them when I went back to sign.

142
00:12:50,120 --> 00:12:51,880
Are you Zheng Yu, in Life Sciences?

143
00:12:51,960 --> 00:12:53,280
I'm not wrong, am I?

144
00:12:53,880 --> 00:12:55,320
Hello, I'm Tang Chenbin.

145
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:57,440
I'm doing an English major.

146
00:12:58,040 --> 00:13:00,040
I saw you in the 3000 m race yesterday.

147
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:05,680
What are these?

148
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:07,240
Did you run the 1500 m too?

149
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:08,160
You're amazing!

150
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:10,760
You have no idea.

151
00:13:10,840 --> 00:13:12,360
I was going to sign up to run,

152
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:15,840
but I was busy working on my thesis
and finding a summer internship,

153
00:13:15,920 --> 00:13:17,560
and had no time to train.

154
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:20,000
Anyway, when I saw you yesterday,

155
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:21,600
I regretted not signing up.

156
00:13:21,680 --> 00:13:23,120
After all, it's my last meet.

157
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:24,840
- This--
- Do you need something?

158
00:13:30,640 --> 00:13:31,640
No.

159
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:32,560
Well…

160
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:34,520
I said so much.

161
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:36,560
Can't you tell that I'm hitting on you?

162
00:13:43,120 --> 00:13:44,040
Well…

163
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:48,040
Can I add you on WeChat?

164
00:14:09,680 --> 00:14:10,520
I'm going to go.

165
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:15,480
I'll send you my info.
Talk to you on WeChat later. Bye.

166
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:21,640
Talk about what?

167
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:23,760
About how to run a marathon?

168
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:33,600
TANG CHENBIN

169
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:35,680
<i>Zheng Yu, are you free this weekend?</i>

170
00:14:36,280 --> 00:14:39,400
<i>There's a maker's market near campus.</i>
<i>Want to go together?</i>

171
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:43,160
How are the edits going on that paper
you worked on with Ms. Cheng?

172
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:45,400
I want to submit it to <i>Molecular Plant,</i>

173
00:14:45,480 --> 00:14:47,240
but my English is limited.

174
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:49,240
I will need help with the translation.

175
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:52,880
Find someone you know.

176
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:55,160
If you find some random person online,

177
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:56,680
they could leak the paper.

178
00:14:57,400 --> 00:14:58,720
Someone I know

179
00:14:58,800 --> 00:15:01,320
who is fluent in English
and knowledgeable about biology

180
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:03,520
is hard to find.

181
00:15:09,120 --> 00:15:11,080
I can think of one person.

182
00:15:11,920 --> 00:15:12,760
Who?

183
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:15,640
TANG CHENBIN
TRANSLATION AND EDITING RATES

184
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:20,240
<i>This is my side gig.</i>

185
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:22,200
<i>Aren't you a senior?</i>

186
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:24,800
<i>If you or your classmates need help,</i>

187
00:15:24,880 --> 00:15:26,240
<i>feel free to contact me.</i>

188
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:28,520
<i>The revisions will be</i>
<i>to your satisfaction.</i>

189
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:36,480
<i>Are you kidding me?</i>

190
00:15:38,880 --> 00:15:39,720
<i>Zheng Yu?</i>

191
00:15:40,520 --> 00:15:41,680
Forget it.

192
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:44,320
You have a paper to revise

193
00:15:44,400 --> 00:15:45,720
and the Excellence Cup,

194
00:15:45,800 --> 00:15:48,400
not to mention all the course assignments.

195
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:50,480
It's clearly a win-win collaboration.

196
00:15:50,560 --> 00:15:52,680
Why do you insist on going at it alone?

197
00:15:52,760 --> 00:15:54,360
You'll just end up like you did last time.

198
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:58,040
Counting the weekend and the Sports Meet,

199
00:15:58,120 --> 00:15:59,680
you had five days off.

200
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:03,160
Everyone seems to have
"post-holiday syndrome."

201
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:04,760
You need something to kick you into gear.

202
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,320
THANK YOU FOR WATCHING
LECTURER: XU KE

203
00:16:06,400 --> 00:16:07,960
This semester's group project

204
00:16:08,040 --> 00:16:09,800
has been posted.

205
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:15,800
For this class, besides attendance,

206
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:19,000
your grade will depend on this assignment.

207
00:16:20,280 --> 00:16:22,000
We have 15 minutes left.

208
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:24,560
Find your group
and decide how to split the work.

209
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:25,760
Get to it.

210
00:16:33,680 --> 00:16:34,880
Zheng Yu,

211
00:16:34,960 --> 00:16:35,960
where is your group?

212
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:37,400
Playing hooky?

213
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:41,360
DID YOU SEE THE ASSIGNMENT?
WHEN SHOULD WE MEET?

214
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:48,640
<i>We should research extension topics</i>
<i>before the next class.</i>

215
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:58,680
SUN DONGCHAO: STILL NEED MORE GAINS

216
00:17:10,359 --> 00:17:11,800
Someone said they work solo,

217
00:17:11,880 --> 00:17:14,319
but in the end, they still had to team up.

218
00:17:15,040 --> 00:17:17,520
And you? Didn't Xu Ke
assign you to a team?

219
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:19,560
I came back from leave.

220
00:17:19,640 --> 00:17:21,319
I don't want to hold others back.

221
00:17:22,800 --> 00:17:26,280
Use the rest of the time in today's class
for group discussions.

222
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:33,880
Zheng Yu, this is
the information I gathered.

223
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:43,800
Besides literature, I also found videos,
so the files are large.

224
00:17:54,720 --> 00:17:56,840
I could have sworn I put the files there.

225
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:04,680
Sun Dongchao, where are your files?

226
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:07,120
I didn't do it.

227
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:08,440
Why do we need so many?

228
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:10,040
Wang Siyun's files are enough.

229
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:12,800
What's up with you?
Zheng Yu and I can't do everything.

230
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:14,680
Let's pick a topic first.

231
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:16,480
Here are my library books.

232
00:18:16,560 --> 00:18:18,080
Fine, I know.

233
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:20,320
I have stuff to do later. I have to go.

234
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,440
You guys can decide.

235
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:27,040
This is too obvious.

236
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:28,720
I'll leave my backpack here.

237
00:18:28,800 --> 00:18:30,520
Bring it to my dorm after class.

238
00:18:30,600 --> 00:18:32,080
Just leave it at the entrance.

239
00:18:32,160 --> 00:18:33,160
We're not done yet.

240
00:18:33,240 --> 00:18:35,080
Don't be a pain. Just help me out.

241
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:36,560
- Fifty yuan.
- Are you broke?

242
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:43,240
<i>I have partnered with others before.</i>

243
00:18:43,320 --> 00:18:44,840
<i>But every time,</i>

244
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:46,240
<i>my partner</i>

245
00:18:46,320 --> 00:18:47,560
<i>was a burden to me.</i>

246
00:19:05,720 --> 00:19:07,160
Can you be more cooperative?

247
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:08,880
This is a group assignment.

248
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:11,320
If you keep this up,
you will piss Zheng Yu off.

249
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:13,400
If she's angry, nobody will do the work.

250
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:15,360
Take a leaf out of my book.

251
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:17,120
Throw together some information

252
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:19,000
and sit back and get a high score.

253
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:20,840
There's nothing to worry about.

254
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:22,760
Xu Ke specified groups of three.

255
00:19:22,840 --> 00:19:24,760
Zheng Yu will have to deal with it.

256
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:25,840
Besides, you and I…

257
00:19:27,720 --> 00:19:28,800
Let's talk over there.

258
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:35,920
You'll take that?

259
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:39,720
I'm used to it.

260
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:51,440
GENE TRANSMISSION

261
00:19:51,520 --> 00:19:53,920
JUNIOR HIGH SCHOOL BIOLOGY
PRACTICE EXAMS

262
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:01,480
<i>The presentation is due</i>
<i>before next week's class.</i>

263
00:20:01,560 --> 00:20:04,280
<i>You can submit the summary</i>
<i>before you present in class.</i>

264
00:20:05,840 --> 00:20:08,640
WANG SIYUN: OK

265
00:20:22,920 --> 00:20:24,720
UNKNOWN NUMBER

266
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:30,080
Hello? Who is it?

267
00:20:30,160 --> 00:20:32,000
<i>I'm outside your dorm building.</i>

268
00:20:32,080 --> 00:20:33,560
<i>I want to talk to you.</i>

269
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:50,800
- What is it?
- Xie Yudi is looking for you.

270
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:52,520
He said he will wait outside.

271
00:20:52,600 --> 00:20:54,480
Maybe you should go see him.

272
00:20:54,560 --> 00:20:55,640
Sorry, I'm busy.

273
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:08,400
There's a guy downstairs
who said he can't reach you.

274
00:21:08,480 --> 00:21:10,040
- He wants to see you.
- Leave it.

275
00:21:11,400 --> 00:21:12,240
I already said…

276
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:14,040
What's wrong?

277
00:21:14,920 --> 00:21:15,920
It's nothing.

278
00:21:23,400 --> 00:21:25,880
I ran into Xie Yudi downstairs just now.

279
00:21:25,960 --> 00:21:28,800
He said he would keep waiting for you.

280
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:31,480
If you don't see him,
he might keep sending people.

281
00:21:31,560 --> 00:21:33,840
Then the whole building will know.

282
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:43,680
What is it?

283
00:21:45,880 --> 00:21:48,760
Sun Dongchao is going around
saying you're a pushover.

284
00:21:48,840 --> 00:21:49,880
Do you know that?

285
00:21:50,520 --> 00:21:52,240
If that's all, I'm going to go.

286
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:56,320
He can do no work in your group
and still get a high score.

287
00:21:56,400 --> 00:21:57,560
Change groups.

288
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:00,800
It's not your concern.

289
00:22:02,840 --> 00:22:03,680
I'm helping you.

290
00:22:03,760 --> 00:22:05,200
Wang Chao is also a slacker.

291
00:22:05,280 --> 00:22:06,720
I'll kick him out. Join us.

292
00:22:06,800 --> 00:22:07,760
No need.

293
00:22:27,920 --> 00:22:29,400
<i>I just saw this.</i>

294
00:22:29,480 --> 00:22:30,440
<i>Forget it.</i>

295
00:22:30,520 --> 00:22:33,040
<i>I'm already swamped</i>
<i>with graduation requirements.</i>

296
00:22:33,120 --> 00:22:35,240
<i>Don't send translation gigs to me.</i>

297
00:22:35,320 --> 00:22:38,240
<i>Graduating earlier will save me a fortune.</i>

298
00:22:38,320 --> 00:22:40,640
<i>I thought I could finish in three years.</i>

299
00:22:40,720 --> 00:22:43,480
<i>Nearly four years in,</i>
<i>graduation isn't even in sight!</i>

300
00:22:43,560 --> 00:22:44,840
QIN SIZHI

301
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:47,120
<i>I must've been crazy to study in Germany.</i>

302
00:22:48,240 --> 00:22:49,400
<i>Are you back at university?</i>

303
00:22:49,480 --> 00:22:51,080
<i>Are you doing better now?</i>

304
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:01,520
ZHENG YU

305
00:23:01,600 --> 00:23:03,400
Genetics problems look complicated,

306
00:23:03,480 --> 00:23:04,800
but there's a trick to it.

307
00:23:04,880 --> 00:23:07,280
Start by drawing a genetic diagram,

308
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:09,800
and identify the parents
and their children.

309
00:23:14,560 --> 00:23:15,480
Keep going.

310
00:23:16,640 --> 00:23:20,440
Now, try to determine whether this trait
is dominant or recessive.

311
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:24,960
Is that your boyfriend?

312
00:23:26,120 --> 00:23:27,320
Focus on the problem.

313
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:29,680
Just send a reply.

314
00:23:29,760 --> 00:23:31,040
I'm tutoring you.

315
00:23:31,640 --> 00:23:33,280
What if they can't reach you

316
00:23:33,360 --> 00:23:34,640
and keep calling you?

317
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:37,160
Won't that interrupt us?

318
00:23:42,680 --> 00:23:44,200
CHEN YANZHOU

319
00:23:44,280 --> 00:23:45,400
<i>Are you on campus?</i>

320
00:23:46,040 --> 00:23:47,160
<i>I need to talk to you.</i>

321
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:50,240
<i>I'm not.</i>

322
00:23:50,320 --> 00:23:52,560
<i>I'll be at the convenience store later.</i>

323
00:23:55,520 --> 00:23:56,400
<i>What time?</i>

324
00:23:57,960 --> 00:23:59,040
<i>Around 5:30 p.m.</i>

325
00:24:01,560 --> 00:24:02,800
Playing on your phone?

326
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:04,640
Is this how you waste time?

327
00:24:04,720 --> 00:24:05,720
No, Mom, it was me--

328
00:24:05,800 --> 00:24:07,160
Be quiet.

329
00:24:08,080 --> 00:24:10,760
Zheng Yu, I hire you by the hour.

330
00:24:10,840 --> 00:24:13,280
Every minute that you waste costs money.

331
00:24:28,200 --> 00:24:30,520
I can extend the lesson
by 10 minutes today.

332
00:24:30,600 --> 00:24:31,880
Is that acceptable?

333
00:24:36,840 --> 00:24:38,280
I'll let it slide this time.

334
00:24:38,360 --> 00:24:39,920
Don't do it again.

335
00:24:43,640 --> 00:24:44,760
I'll check your work.

336
00:25:01,520 --> 00:25:04,280
WHAT TIME?

337
00:25:19,960 --> 00:25:22,680
AROUND 5:30 P.M.

338
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:32,960
CHEN YANZHOU

339
00:26:01,440 --> 00:26:03,280
You're early today.

340
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:24,680
Do you see that boy over there?

341
00:26:25,400 --> 00:26:27,920
He sat here for three hours
and didn't buy a thing.

342
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:29,840
Is this a free study room?

343
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:34,480
Take care of it.

344
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:35,640
I'm leaving.

345
00:26:48,800 --> 00:26:50,200
That's 120 yuan.

346
00:27:01,520 --> 00:27:02,480
For you.

347
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:08,680
What do you want? Tell me.

348
00:27:10,600 --> 00:27:11,640
I want

349
00:27:12,200 --> 00:27:13,040
your help.

350
00:27:14,400 --> 00:27:17,480
I have a paper that needs
to be translated into English.

351
00:27:19,000 --> 00:27:20,760
I'll pay. Name your price.

352
00:27:22,600 --> 00:27:23,640
Okay.

353
00:27:24,400 --> 00:27:25,280
However,

354
00:27:25,880 --> 00:27:27,280
I also need

355
00:27:27,920 --> 00:27:29,040
a favor from you.

356
00:27:31,400 --> 00:27:32,720
Come in.

357
00:27:42,000 --> 00:27:44,400
Sir, I'm Chen Yanzhou
in Life Sciences Class 1.

358
00:27:44,480 --> 00:27:45,320
What do you need?

359
00:27:45,920 --> 00:27:48,240
I was away on medical leave for a year.

360
00:27:48,320 --> 00:27:50,280
Now that I'm back,

361
00:27:50,360 --> 00:27:52,120
I feel quite a bit behind.

362
00:27:52,200 --> 00:27:53,800
I'm catching up too slowly.

363
00:27:53,880 --> 00:27:57,560
I want to team up with a classmate
for the microbiology project.

364
00:27:57,640 --> 00:27:59,440
That is possible,

365
00:27:59,520 --> 00:28:01,920
but groups were already formed
in that class.

366
00:28:02,600 --> 00:28:05,520
If I directly bring in
a classmate for you,

367
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:07,240
others might find out you…

368
00:28:09,200 --> 00:28:10,440
I'll be in a tough spot.

369
00:28:12,520 --> 00:28:13,520
I see.

370
00:28:14,920 --> 00:28:16,880
Or you can see

371
00:28:16,960 --> 00:28:18,920
if anyone will team up with you.

372
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:21,480
If they agree to it, I won't object.

373
00:28:23,400 --> 00:28:24,360
Thank you, sir.

374
00:28:24,440 --> 00:28:25,640
I'll ask around.

375
00:28:25,720 --> 00:28:26,880
I'll message you later.

376
00:28:26,960 --> 00:28:27,880
Okay.

377
00:28:34,640 --> 00:28:35,920
MICROBIOLOGY GROUP

378
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,040
CHAT DETAILS

379
00:28:37,120 --> 00:28:38,440
LEAVE GROUP

380
00:28:38,520 --> 00:28:41,320
Why didn't you just explain
the situation to the teacher?

381
00:28:42,640 --> 00:28:45,040
Xu Ke hates tattletales.

382
00:28:45,120 --> 00:28:46,640
When partners don't get along,

383
00:28:46,720 --> 00:28:49,720
he will believe
that the tattletale is the problem.

384
00:28:52,040 --> 00:28:55,080
I just realized you seem
to know every teacher well.

385
00:28:55,160 --> 00:28:57,640
When Li Yanan paired us up,
you could've refused.

386
00:28:57,720 --> 00:28:59,120
In the football class,

387
00:28:59,200 --> 00:29:01,280
you knew the teacher hates substitutes.

388
00:29:01,360 --> 00:29:03,840
Now, you know
the microbiology teacher's temper.

389
00:29:07,240 --> 00:29:08,240
Know what this is?

390
00:29:09,840 --> 00:29:11,520
Cutting off the head of the snake?

391
00:29:13,560 --> 00:29:15,160
Biological adaptation.

392
00:29:19,360 --> 00:29:20,520
<i>What does this mean?</i>

393
00:29:20,600 --> 00:29:21,480
WANG SIYUN

394
00:29:22,400 --> 00:29:23,360
Bye.

395
00:29:30,040 --> 00:29:30,880
<i>Sir.</i>

396
00:29:33,320 --> 00:29:34,840
What's the problem?

397
00:29:34,920 --> 00:29:36,560
Zheng Yu just suddenly withdrew!

398
00:29:36,640 --> 00:29:38,200
Our assignment was half done.

399
00:29:38,280 --> 00:29:40,640
With her gone,
we don't have time to start over.

400
00:29:40,720 --> 00:29:41,560
Exactly.

401
00:29:41,640 --> 00:29:44,560
We worked hard on it together.
How could she just leave?

402
00:29:44,640 --> 00:29:45,640
I know about this.

403
00:29:46,280 --> 00:29:48,000
I approved her withdrawal.

404
00:29:48,080 --> 00:29:50,000
Sir, this isn't fair.

405
00:29:50,080 --> 00:29:51,120
No, sir.

406
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:53,680
She always carried on
and disregarded our opinions.

407
00:29:53,760 --> 00:29:56,200
Now she has even taken our work with her.

408
00:29:57,120 --> 00:29:58,840
I have spoken to Zheng Yu.

409
00:29:58,920 --> 00:30:02,360
She said she won't
take your group's work with her.

410
00:30:03,080 --> 00:30:05,720
She will start over with other classmates.

411
00:30:05,800 --> 00:30:08,400
Sun Dongchao and Wang Siyun, right?

412
00:30:10,720 --> 00:30:12,400
I remember you two well.

413
00:30:12,480 --> 00:30:13,920
Here, Sun Dongchao.

414
00:30:14,800 --> 00:30:17,480
"Absent, absent, left early,
absent, absent."

415
00:30:17,560 --> 00:30:20,520
In the future,
if you're absent one more time,

416
00:30:20,600 --> 00:30:23,280
you won't get credit for this class.

417
00:30:23,360 --> 00:30:24,720
- Sir, that was--
- Enough.

418
00:30:25,400 --> 00:30:27,800
You're usually sleeping
in class or absent.

419
00:30:27,880 --> 00:30:29,440
Do you think I'm unaware?

420
00:30:29,520 --> 00:30:32,040
So far, Zheng Yu has been
the only one working

421
00:30:32,120 --> 00:30:33,720
on the group assignment, right?

422
00:30:33,800 --> 00:30:35,320
I didn't want to interfere.

423
00:30:35,400 --> 00:30:38,440
You're all adults,
not elementary school kids.

424
00:30:38,520 --> 00:30:41,480
I believed you guys
could sort it out among yourselves.

425
00:30:42,080 --> 00:30:43,360
But now,

426
00:30:43,440 --> 00:30:46,120
you're complaining about her
and speaking ill of her.

427
00:30:46,800 --> 00:30:47,640
Let's do this.

428
00:30:48,880 --> 00:30:49,960
You two are a group.

429
00:30:50,560 --> 00:30:54,400
Submit your slides and summary
to me separately for review.

430
00:31:06,560 --> 00:31:08,040
What are you doing?

431
00:31:08,120 --> 00:31:09,160
Give it to me.

432
00:31:15,760 --> 00:31:17,000
It looks nice.

433
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:20,800
ZHENG YU

434
00:31:20,880 --> 00:31:21,960
<i>When are you free?</i>

435
00:31:22,040 --> 00:31:24,120
<i>Let's split up</i>
<i>the microbiology assignment.</i>

436
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:25,920
<i>Tomorrow morning.</i>

437
00:31:26,000 --> 00:31:27,080
<i>Let's go to the library.</i>

438
00:31:27,840 --> 00:31:28,800
<i>Okay.</i>

439
00:31:50,800 --> 00:31:53,200
Your seat choices sure are unconventional.

440
00:31:53,800 --> 00:31:55,000
How will we communicate?

441
00:31:56,080 --> 00:31:57,640
The seats next to you

442
00:31:57,720 --> 00:31:59,680
were reserved by others.

443
00:32:00,760 --> 00:32:03,520
If necessary, we'll communicate on WeChat.

444
00:32:14,160 --> 00:32:15,360
Let's leave.

445
00:32:15,440 --> 00:32:17,480
There's another place that is available.

446
00:32:34,720 --> 00:32:37,000
No one uses this lab anymore.

447
00:32:37,640 --> 00:32:39,080
How did you get the key?

448
00:32:39,840 --> 00:32:41,320
Did Mr. Li give it to you?

449
00:32:42,720 --> 00:32:44,800
What? Suspect that I bribed him again?

450
00:32:50,040 --> 00:32:51,760
Mr. Li and my mom are old friends,

451
00:32:51,840 --> 00:32:54,160
so he does look after me.

452
00:32:54,240 --> 00:32:56,320
But he has always
been impartial professionally.

453
00:32:56,400 --> 00:32:59,120
If you ask him for the key,
he will give it to you too.

454
00:33:00,200 --> 00:33:01,840
I didn't say anything.

455
00:33:10,080 --> 00:33:11,200
Come in.

456
00:33:31,400 --> 00:33:33,760
Did you grow this thale cress?

457
00:33:34,560 --> 00:33:35,920
Keep this a secret.

458
00:33:38,800 --> 00:33:40,000
You can sit here.

459
00:33:53,840 --> 00:33:55,200
How far along are you?

460
00:33:55,280 --> 00:33:57,920
The presentation is done.
Just the summary is left.

461
00:33:58,000 --> 00:33:59,680
I can do the summary.

462
00:33:59,760 --> 00:34:00,600
No need.

463
00:34:00,680 --> 00:34:02,960
Just translate and revise my paper.

464
00:34:03,040 --> 00:34:04,160
I will add your name

465
00:34:04,240 --> 00:34:06,360
to the microbiology assignment.

466
00:34:07,040 --> 00:34:08,760
Those are two different things.

467
00:34:09,360 --> 00:34:10,960
I'll finish the report in time.

468
00:34:11,040 --> 00:34:12,719
I won't take any advantage of you.

469
00:34:18,040 --> 00:34:20,120
Send me the information later.

470
00:34:20,199 --> 00:34:23,679
Click this link to see me
writing the report in real time.

471
00:34:23,760 --> 00:34:25,880
If anything doesn't match, point it out.

472
00:34:27,360 --> 00:34:28,360
Why bother?

473
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:32,040
It's no trouble.
Everything should be clear.

474
00:34:32,120 --> 00:34:32,960
SEND

475
00:34:36,679 --> 00:34:37,920
These are my rates.

476
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:40,840
Since you helped me change groups,

477
00:34:41,360 --> 00:34:42,760
I can give you a discount.

478
00:34:44,800 --> 00:34:46,920
Did you make this list just for me?

479
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:48,120
It's my side gig.

480
00:34:49,800 --> 00:34:51,840
How many people have you sent it to?

481
00:34:51,920 --> 00:34:54,000
Has everyone in the college received it?

482
00:34:54,080 --> 00:34:57,400
I've sent it to our college
and the College of Foreign Languages.

483
00:34:57,480 --> 00:35:00,120
Especially students doing English majors.
My English is pretty good.

484
00:35:02,800 --> 00:35:03,880
English majors?

485
00:35:05,280 --> 00:35:08,280
Did you befriend that
English major student at the cafeteria

486
00:35:08,360 --> 00:35:10,120
just to advertise yourself?

487
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:13,120
Why else?

488
00:35:27,240 --> 00:35:29,080
ZHENG YU

489
00:35:39,080 --> 00:35:40,800
GOT IT

490
00:35:55,000 --> 00:35:56,440
WPS CLOUD DOCUMENT

491
00:35:59,600 --> 00:36:01,320
HUMAN ENDOGENOUS RETROVIRUSES…

492
00:36:06,200 --> 00:36:08,440
DYNAMIC EXPRESSION
OF HUMAN ENDOGENOUS…

493
00:36:12,080 --> 00:36:17,560
SUMMARY OF RESULTS

494
00:36:33,600 --> 00:36:36,760
BASED ON THE DYNAMIC ACTIVATION PATTERN,
VIRAL GENE ACTIVITY…

495
00:36:41,880 --> 00:36:42,920
CHEN YANZHOU

496
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:47,000
NOT BAD.

497
00:36:56,960 --> 00:36:58,360
GOT IT.

498
00:37:22,040 --> 00:37:24,480
…CRUCIAL FOR
UNDERSTANDING…

499
00:37:27,720 --> 00:37:29,120
…INDIVIDUAL
GENETIC DIVERSITY…

500
00:37:34,560 --> 00:37:36,280
NOT EATING DINNER?

501
00:37:44,240 --> 00:37:45,880
It's divided into four stages.

502
00:37:45,960 --> 00:37:47,880
The first stage is uptake.

503
00:37:48,440 --> 00:37:51,160
Antigen-presenting cells,
commonly known as APCs,

504
00:37:51,240 --> 00:37:53,600
use mechanisms
like phagocytosis and pinocytosis

505
00:37:53,680 --> 00:37:55,680
to engulf extracellular antigens.

506
00:38:03,360 --> 00:38:05,080
LOOK UP

507
00:38:08,320 --> 00:38:09,880
The second stage is processing.

508
00:38:10,840 --> 00:38:14,120
After antigens in the body
fuse with lysosomes.

509
00:38:14,200 --> 00:38:17,400
They are broken down into short peptides
of 13 to 20 amino acids.

510
00:38:24,680 --> 00:38:27,600
Next group, Zheng Yu and Chen Yanzhou.

511
00:38:30,160 --> 00:38:33,000
THANK YOU FOR WATCHING

512
00:38:39,240 --> 00:38:42,040
Have you thought about
where human genes come from?

513
00:38:43,120 --> 00:38:44,360
Your father or mother?

514
00:38:44,440 --> 00:38:46,480
Or maybe from an ancient virus.

515
00:38:46,560 --> 00:38:47,720
In 2016,

516
00:38:47,800 --> 00:38:50,560
researchers at the University of Michigan
Medical School

517
00:38:50,640 --> 00:38:52,880
studied over 2500 human genomes.

518
00:38:52,960 --> 00:38:56,600
Thirty-six viral genes were found
lurking in the human genome.

519
00:38:56,680 --> 00:39:00,560
Among them, 19 types were
newly discovered and newly identified

520
00:39:00,640 --> 00:39:02,720
DNA fragments from viruses.

521
00:39:18,920 --> 00:39:21,280
FIRST SEMESTER ATTENDANCE SHEET

522
00:39:24,480 --> 00:39:26,600
35% OF WORKING PROFESSIONALS
NEVER SWITCH PHONES OFF…

523
00:39:31,160 --> 00:39:32,880
- Registered for the cup yet?
- No.

524
00:39:34,240 --> 00:39:35,440
Eight yuan.

525
00:39:35,520 --> 00:39:36,920
Everyone else has signed up.

526
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:38,000
It costs 800 yuan.

527
00:39:38,080 --> 00:39:39,840
The collage will reimburse you

528
00:39:39,920 --> 00:39:41,680
if you get a ranking in the finals.

529
00:39:41,760 --> 00:39:43,480
There's also the prize money.

530
00:39:43,560 --> 00:39:44,400
And if I don't?

531
00:39:45,520 --> 00:39:46,840
So little confidence?

532
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:49,200
Want to work with me?

533
00:39:52,600 --> 00:39:55,480
I'll pay the registration fee.
It'll be reimbursed anyway.

534
00:39:56,120 --> 00:39:58,320
I want to free up time
for my own research.

535
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:00,920
Don't worry.

536
00:40:01,000 --> 00:40:03,320
You won't lose out by working with me.

537
00:40:03,400 --> 00:40:04,920
I won't hold you back.

538
00:40:05,000 --> 00:40:07,240
If I remember correctly,

539
00:40:07,320 --> 00:40:11,080
you just learned
to put on rollerblades and move slowly.

540
00:40:14,560 --> 00:40:15,440
Excluding that.

541
00:40:16,400 --> 00:40:19,240
Besides, there are
no group projects in that class.

542
00:40:19,320 --> 00:40:21,360
Even if I fail, it won't affect you.

543
00:40:21,960 --> 00:40:24,360
Others have been preparing
for nearly two months.

544
00:40:24,440 --> 00:40:26,560
Isn't it too late for us to start now?

545
00:40:27,600 --> 00:40:29,280
I've already chosen a topic.

546
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:31,760
Based on my understanding of you,

547
00:40:31,840 --> 00:40:32,680
the two of us

548
00:40:32,760 --> 00:40:35,240
will be able to keep up with each other.

549
00:40:35,960 --> 00:40:37,640
Registration will end soon.

550
00:40:38,400 --> 00:40:39,720
Do you dare to go for it?

551
00:40:40,440 --> 00:40:41,840
Your understanding of me?

552
00:40:42,400 --> 00:40:43,240
What do you know?

553
00:40:51,520 --> 00:40:52,520
I can agree to it,

554
00:40:52,600 --> 00:40:54,720
but you have to cover lab material costs

555
00:40:54,800 --> 00:40:56,280
during the competition.

556
00:40:57,200 --> 00:41:00,000
Also, I want to borrow two books from you.

557
00:41:00,600 --> 00:41:02,400
Consider it your show of good faith.

558
00:41:02,480 --> 00:41:04,480
Doesn't the library have those books?

559
00:41:04,560 --> 00:41:05,640
Anyway, you have them.

560
00:41:06,320 --> 00:41:07,200
How do you know?

561
00:41:07,280 --> 00:41:09,080
You brought them to the library.

562
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:12,280
You peeked at my books?

563
00:41:31,120 --> 00:41:32,920
<i>Rollerblading basics.</i>

564
00:41:33,720 --> 00:41:35,880
<i>Part one. The starting position.</i>

565
00:41:36,400 --> 00:41:38,600
<i>Have your feet shoulder-width apart</i>

566
00:41:38,680 --> 00:41:41,840
<i>with toes pointing slightly outward.</i>

567
00:41:43,000 --> 00:41:44,600
<i>Bend your knees forward</i>

568
00:41:44,680 --> 00:41:46,000
<i>but don't lock them.</i>

569
00:41:46,080 --> 00:41:47,840
<i>Lower your hips slightly.</i>

570
00:41:49,960 --> 00:41:51,440
Here are the books you wanted.

571
00:42:12,600 --> 00:42:14,120
Use this to record later.

572
00:42:14,200 --> 00:42:16,520
It has the data from previous experiments.

573
00:42:20,080 --> 00:42:22,640
KEY EXPERIMENTAL METHODS
TABLE OF EXPERIMENTAL DATA

574
00:42:22,720 --> 00:42:24,800
BASIC TECHNIQUES OF ROLLERBLADING

575
00:42:28,960 --> 00:42:30,000
What is it?

576
00:42:31,600 --> 00:42:32,760
Nothing.

577
00:42:41,400 --> 00:42:43,960
Since you carried
all these books to campus,

578
00:42:44,040 --> 00:42:46,600
I'll give you a tip
to pass the rollerblading exam.

579
00:42:48,720 --> 00:42:49,720
Do tell.

580
00:42:51,160 --> 00:42:54,840
Prepare a move that the teacher doesn't
ask for and save it for last.

581
00:42:54,920 --> 00:42:56,760
It's okay if you haven't mastered it.

582
00:42:56,840 --> 00:43:00,680
An upperclassman said that
the teacher will give extra points.

583
00:43:03,320 --> 00:43:04,400
Got it.

584
00:43:06,240 --> 00:43:07,280
Bye.

585
00:43:10,760 --> 00:43:12,440
- I'll buy you dinner.
- No, thanks.

586
00:43:12,520 --> 00:43:14,360
See you at the lab this weekend.

587
00:43:18,960 --> 00:43:20,840
Guess you'll have to settle for me.

588
00:43:29,040 --> 00:43:30,240
So there's a chance.

589
00:43:32,880 --> 00:43:34,240
What are you talking about?

590
00:43:34,320 --> 00:43:35,160
You and Zheng Yu.

591
00:43:36,040 --> 00:43:39,120
I never expected you two to sign up
for the Excellence Cup together.

592
00:43:40,120 --> 00:43:42,680
I originally didn't plan
to compete together.

593
00:43:43,680 --> 00:43:45,280
What changed your mind?

594
00:43:45,960 --> 00:43:48,960
We worked together in microbiology,
and it wasn't bad.

595
00:43:49,040 --> 00:43:52,280
I told you. You two just hadn't tried yet.

596
00:43:53,120 --> 00:43:54,240
But I'm curious.

597
00:43:54,320 --> 00:43:56,360
Which of you reached out first?

598
00:43:59,520 --> 00:44:01,240
Who reached out first?

599
00:44:03,960 --> 00:44:04,840
Who cares?

600
00:44:05,640 --> 00:44:06,560
I actually think

601
00:44:07,120 --> 00:44:08,880
you two are quite similar.

602
00:44:09,520 --> 00:44:12,360
You're both quite indifferent
to others around you.

603
00:44:12,440 --> 00:44:14,760
But you hold nothing back in your studies.

604
00:44:14,840 --> 00:44:16,200
That enthusiasm is like

605
00:44:16,800 --> 00:44:18,280
a ball of fire in your hand.

606
00:44:19,400 --> 00:44:21,360
That absolute devotion gives others--

607
00:44:21,440 --> 00:44:22,800
Hot!

608
00:44:26,680 --> 00:44:29,800
I believe you two will get nice results.

609
00:44:31,400 --> 00:44:32,520
I sure hope so.

610
00:44:40,720 --> 00:44:42,080
I'm quite curious.

611
00:44:42,960 --> 00:44:45,280
Zheng Yu has good grades and capabilities.

612
00:44:45,360 --> 00:44:49,440
Why hasn't she ever joined a lab
or done research?

613
00:44:50,040 --> 00:44:53,240
She always seems to be busy
with unimportant things.

614
00:44:53,840 --> 00:44:55,120
Do you want to know?

615
00:44:56,360 --> 00:44:57,200
Ask her.

616
00:44:58,840 --> 00:45:01,440
That's how relationships are established.

617
00:45:02,040 --> 00:45:04,480
That's also how friends are made.

618
00:45:05,160 --> 00:45:06,120
Friends?

619
00:45:09,040 --> 00:45:10,800
We're just ordinary classmates.

620
00:45:17,240 --> 00:45:18,440
Thank you.

621
00:45:18,520 --> 00:45:19,440
Let's go.

622
00:45:32,400 --> 00:45:34,280
